`Nautilus.TimeSeries.ts_ewma_series` argument 1: expected f32, got f64

Blocker: the Nautilus.TimeSeries EWMA entry is f32-only (nautilus#70).
This is a capability probe for that named entry, not for the independent
Nautilus.Rolling f64 list and tensor operations supplied by resolved
nautilus#85. Shoals's rolling wrappers use Nautilus.Rolling and retain
Shoals's complete-window mask, Option results, Ddof mapping, and lag guards.

DE-NARROWING: if this probe passes because TimeSeries admits f64, promote it
to a normal cross-width test and archive the remaining nautilus#70 entry in
docs/UPSTREAM_BUGS.md. Check the actual exported EWMA signature and behavior
before reusing it; a passing EWMA probe does not replace the distinct rolling
and lag equivalence, warm-up, and negative-domain tests.
